From klofstad-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org  Wed Jul  7 15:22:11 2010
From: klofstad-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org (Casey Klofstad)
Date: Wed, 07 Jul 2010 11:22:11 -0400
Subject: specify more than one value in setx
Message-ID: <AANLkTinZaX6__r7Tnj5sZzAO7Fquzuspi54LMTxUyhjj@mail.gmail.com>

Hey all-

Can someone explain how to specify the value of more than one variable
in setx? For example, I have a model with predicts y with b1 b2 and
b3. In this example, how could I set b1 = 1, b2 = 0 and b3 = mean?

Thanks much,

-c

