From plam-fWAZDB8bsKe+fmr0zi+kZQ at public.gmane.org  Wed Jul  7 19:00:53 2010
From: plam-fWAZDB8bsKe+fmr0zi+kZQ at public.gmane.org (Patrick Lam)
Date: Wed, 07 Jul 2010 15:00:53 -0400
Subject: Re: specify more than one value in setx
In-Reply-To: <AANLkTinZaX6__r7Tnj5sZzAO7Fquzuspi54LMTxUyhjj@mail.gmail.com>
References: <AANLkTinZaX6__r7Tnj5sZzAO7Fquzuspi54LMTxUyhjj@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <AANLkTimM3GZUhuV-b25DBpyLxjBfUoN2-K3ohPNvBZv9@mail.gmail.com>

Casey,

You can do this in setx() with just

setx(z.out, b1=1, b2=0, b3=mean(data$b3))

Also, if b3 is a numeric variable, then setx automatically defaults to the
mean and you don't have to respecify it.

